Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 08:03:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Fix selection-changed notify guard and add
 deselect->empty-panel regression test

- D3GraphEditor.notifySelectionChanged: guard on the callback's existence
  (`if (this.selectionChangedCallback)`) instead of invoking it inside the
  condition and again in the body. The old form double-invoked the callback
  when it returned truthy and would throw if no callback were registered;
  now consistent with notifyGraphChanged.
- Add core-features e2e "should return the right panel to empty selection when
  deselecting a layer": selects a layer (params shown, overview hidden), clicks
  empty canvas to deselect, asserts the right panel returns to the Network
  Overview empty state and the node loses its selected class. Verified it fails
  when selection notification is disabled.
- Check off the corresponding item in docs/tasks.md.

Verified: lint 0/0, 25 unit tests, build ok, new e2e passes (and fails when the
feature is broken).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
